      "type": "引用",
      "type_label": "引用",
      "text": "SpaceX will attempt to catch both the Super Heavy booster and Starship on the upcoming flight. \n\nIf both are successful, it will mark the first time that all parts of an orbital rocket return to Earth intact. \n\nThis is the critical breakthrough needed to make life multiplanetary.",
      "quote": {
        "author": "SpaceX",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1697749409851985920/HbrI04tM_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-06 22:56:55",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-11-06T14:56:55.000Z",
        "id": "2118719281038770389",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2118716025151619072/img/dtsnQSn9XFLasn6P.jpg"
        ],
        "media": [
          {
            "duration": 1270.31,
            "height": 2160,
            "thumbnail_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2118716025151619072/img/dtsnQSn9XFLasn6P.jpg",
            "type": "video",
            "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2118716025151619072/vid/avc1/3840x2160/JJB5HQJWGXUeFC1r.mp4?tag=29",
            "width": 3840
          }
        ],
        "name": "SpaceX",
        "text": "More than a dozen flight tests and years of development, with countless hours worked by SpaceX engineers and technicians, all come down to this: the first orbital Starship launch carrying advanced Starlink satellites bound for space. \n\nWatch “Go For Orbit” and experience the moments behind flying the most ambitious Starship mission yet",
        "url": "https://x.com/SpaceX/status/2118719281038770389",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "organization"
      },
